  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It builds a forest with a seeded RNG and three instanced nodes: 8,000 trunks, 8,000 canopies and 2,000 rocks. That makes 8,000 trees plus 2,000 rocks, 10,000 objects, with no per-object meshes. Canopies and rocks get per-instance HSL colours. The scene has a ground plane, one shadow-casting directional light (4096 map fitted to the forest) and exponential fog. The camera is orbited slowly from onFrame via `app.camera.setPose`, at radius 100 and height 55. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frames. The typecheck passes, but I couldn't run it in a browser here, so the shadow fit, fog density and camera framing are untested.",
